═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
PART 3: ANALYSIS
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

3.1 WHAT WORKED
──────────────────────────────────────
✓ Pattern detection — correctly identified threshold clustering
✓ Predicate generation — created valid Python predicate
✓ Tree generation — created valid .vsm tree
✓ Component registration — registered in system
✓ Validation — checked syntax before registration

3.2 LIMITATIONS
──────────────────────────────────────
✗ Single pattern type — only detected threshold_clustering
✗ No dynamic generation — generates new components, not modify existing
✗ No performance tracking — doesn't track generated component performance
✗ No rollback — can't revert to previous components

3.3 LESSONS LEARNED
──────────────────────────────────────
1. Pattern detection is critical — identifies where to generate
2. Component generation is straightforward — template-based approach works
3. Registration prevents duplicates — important for system stability
4. Validation is essential — prevents broken components from entering system

